WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.947
Checkpoint 1 focuses on recognition.

00:00:02.947 --> 00:00:07.952
Classify each variable as nominal, ordinal, interval, or ratio.

00:00:07.952 --> 00:00:14.332
For numeric variables, also decide whether the concept is counted or measured.

00:00:14.332 --> 00:00:19.632
Try to answer before opening the sample classifications.

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:27.047
If you are unsure, return to the questions: label or quantity, ordered or unordered, true zero or not,

00:00:27.047 --> 00:00:34.357
counted or measured. For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:34.357 --> 00:00:40.357
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:40.357 --> 00:00:42.747
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:48.787
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:48.787 --> 00:00:55.912
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:55.912 --> 00:01:03.482
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:01:03.482 --> 00:01:08.320
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
